# Piano (Xiaomi Pad 8 Pro) kernel config fragment
#
# The stock GKI 6.6.118 kernel on this device is built with
#
#     # CONFIG_VT is not set
#
# so there is no virtual terminal and no /dev/tty0.  That is fine for Android,
# but it blocks one thing on the Linux side: KWin / weston / sway cannot use
# their DRM backend.  libseat insists on opening /dev/tty0 to bind the session
# to a VT, and with no VT support the kernel never creates that node, so the
# compositor aborts with "Could not open tty0" / "Failed to open VT".
#
# Applied on top of the device's own config so the shipped baseline stays
# untouched:
#
#     cp /proc/config.gz-derived config to .config
#     make ARCH=arm64 olddefconfig
#     scripts/kconfig/merge_config.sh -m .config \
#         arch/arm64/configs/piano_gki.fragment
#     make ARCH=arm64 olddefconfig
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Why only VT, and not fbcon / the boot logo
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Turning on CONFIG_FB + CONFIG_FRAMEBUFFER_CONSOLE + CONFIG_DRM_FBDEV_EMULATION
# + CONFIG_LOGO produces a kernel that boots and creates /dev/tty0, but Android
# then never comes up: SurfaceFlinger dies in a crash loop with
#
#     SDM: HWInfoDRM::Init: Failed to acquire DRMMaster instance 0
#     SurfaceFlinger: Initial display configuration failed: HWC did not hotplug
#
# The cause is not vermagic but symbol CRCs.  CONFIG_MODVERSIONS=y makes the
# module loader compare every symbol CRC in the module's __versions section
# against the kernel's.  DRM_FBDEV_EMULATION changes the layout of struct
# drm_device / drm_framebuffer, which changes the CRC of every DRM symbol, so
# msm_drm.ko refuses to load:
#
#     msm_drm: disagrees about version of symbol drm_panel_init
#     msm_drm: disagrees about version of symbol backlight_device_register
#
# Measured on this device:
#
#     symbol                            with FBDEV    without     vendor expects
#     backlight_device_register         0x1a91d54c    0x2dbddc88  0x2dbddc88
#     drm_panel_init                    0x9b7c3085    0xac1477ea  0xac1477ea
#     drm_helper_mode_fill_fb_struct    0x60cf208e    0xbe13fdf0  0xbe13fdf0
#     module_layout                     0x4e276f37    0x4e276f37  0x4e276f37
#
# Note module_layout matches either way: the base ABI is fine and vermagic is
# irrelevant here.  Only the DRM symbols move.
#
# CONFIG_VT on its own touches no DRM structure at all, so /dev/tty0 appears
# and Android boots normally.
#
# The cost is that kernel log output during boot is no longer drawn on the
# panel.  On this device that was never going to work anyway: boot goes through
# Android, where composer/SurfaceFlinger owns the display, and the panel is a
# dual-DSI 1600x2136 half-panel that plain fbcon would not drive correctly.
# Use ramoops instead (already configured on this device, 2 MB console buffer,
# readable from /sys/fs/pstore/ after a reboot), or kmscon on the Linux side.

# --- virtual terminal -------------------------------------------------------
# This is the whole point: CONFIG_VT is what creates /dev/tty0 .. /dev/tty63.
CONFIG_VT=y
CONFIG_VT_CONSOLE=y
CONFIG_HW_CONSOLE=y
CONFIG_DUMMY_CONSOLE=y
# UNIX98 ptys are already enabled in gki_defconfig; restated so this fragment
# is self-contained if it is ever merged into a different baseline.
CONFIG_UNIX98_PTYS=y

# --- deliberately left off --------------------------------------------------
# Each of these drags in the fbdev core and/or changes DRM structure layout,
# which breaks msm_drm.ko's symbol CRCs.  See the long comment above.
# CONFIG_FB is not set
# CONFIG_FRAMEBUFFER_CONSOLE is not set
# CONFIG_DRM_FBDEV_EMULATION is not set
# CONFIG_LOGO is not set

# --- do not trim exported symbols -------------------------------------------
# Android GKI defaults to CONFIG_TRIM_UNUSED_KSYMS=y with the whitelist
# abi_symbollist.raw, a file that Kleaf generates from the real ABI definition.
# This tree has no Kleaf step, so the file would have to be faked -- and a
# hand-assembled whitelist is nowhere near complete.  Measured: trimming drops
# the kernel from 16579 exported symbols to 3576, and every vendor_dlkm module
# that links against a dropped symbol then fails to load.  The known-booting
# kernel_platform build has trimming off, so match it.
# CONFIG_TRIM_UNUSED_KSYMS is not set

# --- kernel release string ---------------------------------------------------
# The vendor modules on this device were built against the exact release string
# of the shipped GKI kernel:
#
#   6.6.118-android15-8-gf72a02f47f4b-abogki551678766-4k
#
# Pinning it keeps uname -r and dmesg comparable with the stock kernel.  It is
# NOT required for module loading: kernel/module/version.c's same_magic() skips
# everything up to the first space when the module carries CRCs, so only
# "SMP preempt mod_unload modversions aarch64" is actually compared.
CONFIG_LOCALVERSION="-android15-8-gf72a02f47f4b-abogki551678766-4k"
# CONFIG_LOCALVERSION_AUTO is not set

# IMPORTANT: pass LOCALVERSION= (empty) on the make command line.
#
# scripts/setlocalversion has this at the end:
#
#     elif [ "${LOCALVERSION+set}" != "set" ]; then
#             # If the variable LOCALVERSION is not set, append a plus sign
#             scm_version="$(scm_version --short)"
#     fi
#
# CONFIG_LOCALVERSION (the .config symbol) is NOT the make variable
# LOCALVERSION.  If the make variable is unset, setlocalversion appends a
# literal "+" to the release string -- and since this tree is a shallow import
# with no reachable tags, it always takes that path.  The result is
#
#     6.6.118-android15-8-gf72a02f47f4b-abogki551678766-4k+
#
# Passing LOCALVERSION= on the command line counts as "set" and suppresses the
# "+".  Harmless either way (same_magic ignores the prefix), but it keeps
# uname -r tidy:
#
#     make ARCH=arm64 CC=clang LLVM=1 LOCALVERSION= -j8 Image
#
# Also note: after editing CONFIG_LOCALVERSION, include/config/auto.conf is
# stale and kernelrelease keeps the old value.  Clear it:
#
#     rm -f include/config/auto.conf include/config/auto.conf.cmd \
#           include/config/kernel.release
#     make ARCH=arm64 CC=clang LLVM=1 LOCALVERSION= syncconfig
